sopotamia, and China, it was one of the four centres of the ancient world; it was geographically larger than ancient Egypt and Mesopotamia combined. It spanned much of Pakistan, northwestern India, and northeast Afghanistan. The civilisation flourished in the alluvial plain of the Indus River and along a system of perennial monsoon-fed rivers that once coursed in the vicinity of the Ghaggar-Hakra, a seasonal river in northwest India and eastern Pakistan.\nThe term Harappan is also applied to the Indus Civilisation, after its type site Harappa, the first to be excavated early in the 20th century in what was then the Punjab province of British India and is now Punjab, Pakistan."}],"facts":[],"people":{},"media":{},"names":["Civilisation de l'Indus","Civilisation de la vallee de l'Indus","Civilisation de la vallée de l’Indus","Civilisation harappéenne","Civilizacion del Indus","Civilizacion del Valle del Indo","Civilización del Indus","Civilización del valle del Indo","Civilizatio Vallis Indi","Civilização do Indus","Civilização do Vale do Indo","Civilização do Vale do Indus","Civilização do indo","Civilização harappeana","Civilizações do vale do Indo","Civiltà dell'Indo","Civiltà dell'Indo-Sarasvati","Civiltà di Harappa","Cultura del Indo","Cywilizacja Indusu","Cywilizacja doliny Indusu","Harapano","Harappa-Kultur","Harappacultuur","Harappakultur","Harappan Civilization","Harrapaanse beschaving","IVC","Indus Vadisi medeniyeti","Indus Valley Civilisation","Indus Valley Civilization","Indus-Kultur","Indus-Zivilisation","Indus-beschaving","Indus-cultuur","Indusbeschaving","Induscultuur","Induskultur","Indusvallei beschaving","Indusvalleibeschaving","Kultura Indusu","Kultura doliny Indusu","Periodo harappan","Sindhu-Sarasvati traditie","Vale do Indo","Vale do Indus","Valle de Indo","Valle dell'Indo","civilisation de la vallée de l'Indus","civilización del valle del Indo","civiltà della valle dell'Indo","İndus Uygarlığı","İndus Vadisi Uygarlığı","Πολιτισμός της κοιλάδας το